# Galaxy S26 RFGL80R6A6H: filled prompt, allocated KV 2304 / 4096 / 8192.
# ROUNDS=8 COOLDOWN=30 THERMAL_WAIT=600 BENCH_CPU_MASK= BENCH_ANDROID_SERIAL=RFGL80R6A6H
# python3 android/bench/run_campaign.py THIS.cells --dry-run
# Remove --dry-run only in an authorized device round with the shared hold.
# One launch/cell/round; full order reverses on even rounds, anchor once/round.
# LiteRT context prompts: v0.16.0 advanced_main, two fresh Conversations in one
# engine (cold, warm), engine-default sampler, native output cap 256.
# llama.cpp b8999 control: existing llama-cli -st, cold-process only.
# Real prompt counts are authoritative; no synthetic prefill/decode override.
# Exact artifacts match the Mac leg, expressed as Android repo + file=.
# Standard Gemma files (wNa8o8), not the separate -gpu files.
# Qwen3 1.7B cpu = dynamic INT8; gpu = dynamic wi4b32, as on the dashboard.
# Qwen3 0.6B ladder = published wi4b32; mixed_int4 stays an explicit exclusion.
# S26 stored inventory: 12 GB RAM; conservative 60% = 6866 MiB (decimal GB).
# Mac memoryPeakResidentMB excludes E4B CPU 8192 (max 11306 MiB).
# Borderline CPU rows and E4B GPU 8192 require the later smoke, not a RAM claim.
# Full matrix is a plan; prefer the model files for separate sittings (see run
# results/r2_time_estimate.md for target/proposed round counts and sources).

android llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF short-chat anchor=1 runs=1 file=Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf

